# sites-641.draft.kzs -- DRAFT logical sites of case C5 (nasa/cFE #72) for the instrumented family (kzs-sites 2,
# kairos/docs/event_semantics.md section 3) on the pre-fix release cFE 6.4.1 with OSAL 4.1.1 (posix) and the pc-linux
# PSP 1.2.0.0, built as the release readme says (research/cfs_procrace/plan/c5_execution_basis_20261028.md section 2).
# DRAFT: not used by any run.  Checked only by a single-unit compile with kzgcc 0.2 (that plan, section 6.3).  There is
# no F0 counterpart yet (the F0 observer reads only ELF64 x86-64 files, the plan's section 7), so no equiv line.
#
# Paths are relative to the release tree cFE-6.4.1-OSS-release/ (sha256 ec26e33b...) with osal-4.1.1-release moved
# to osal/ (sha256 8f0f2b23...).  Line numbers are those of the files in these tarballs.  Event names E5-* are those
# of plan/case_setup_C2_C3_C5.md section 4.3.  Values are the operands the original code uses (call arguments,
# results, stored values, the enclosing function's parameters) and an out parameter read by the same thread right
# after a call (event_semantics.md 8.1).  The binary is 32-bit (-m32), so pointers and pthread_t are 4 bytes.
# Nothing here is a research condition.
kzs-sites 2
source cfe rev=cFE-6.4.1-OSS-release ref="SourceForge coreflightexec cFE-6.4.1-OSS-release.tar.gz sha256 ec26e33b4ab40b9616ccdbc984c5a00a790a7d05b260f2628c3335a29c23e98f"
source osal rev=osal-4.1.1-release ref="SourceForge osal osal-4.1.1-release.tar.gz sha256 8f0f2b23d8226256fdb8543bf9fcb560b38434411dc12cb4f7f35b9c19e61d46"
module 1 name=core-linux.bin source=cfe
module 2 name=sample_app.so source=cfe

# ---- creator: CFE_ES_AppCreate (cfe_es_apps.c:426-718), E5-UNLOCK / E5-CREATE / E5-RELOCK / E5-PUB ---------------
# The application's slot i is chosen inside the call (L449-L460) and first appears as an operand at L651 and L657,
# after the task is created; so no owner-request can be read before the spawn (plan section 5.2, engine item E-ID1).
# E-ID1 draft (2026-10-29; plan/c5_execution_basis_20261028.md section 10.4).  Comments only: these readers are not
# in kzs-sites 2 and the parser would refuse them.  The owner value is read where the request hands the new slot to
# its caller (L657), not from the analysed TaskTable store (L651, site 8), which is kept as a cross-check only.
#   identity 1 decoder=app-request ref="cfe_es_apps.c:426 (the request creates the application it names later)"
#   site 33 label=es.app_create.owner_out op=es.app_create phase=point place=store line=657 tu=cfe/fsw/cfe-core/src/es/cfe_es_apps.c func=CFE_ES_AppCreate ref="cfe_es_apps.c:657 *ApplicationIdPtr = i"
#   value 33 0 role=app_id from=operand0 type=u32
#   identity 33 decoder=owner-publish owner=0 ref="cfe_es_apps.c:657"
#   identity 2 decoder=request-return status=0 ok=0 ref="CFE_SUCCESS"
