# ---- new task: registration in OSAL and in ES (E5-REG) ------------------------------------------------------------
# OSAL 4.1.1 passes the application's entry function straight to pthread_create (osapi.c:645-648): there is no OSAL
# entry wrapper and no id argument.  The first place where the task names its OSAL id is OS_TaskRegister, which finds
# it by searching OS_task_table for pthread_self() (L916-L927) and stores it as thread-specific data (L938).  Events
# of the task before that keep their actor and are joined afterwards (plan section 5.3).
